; CPF merge for mirror member A of stack 3 - the instance that will become the
; first failover member, and therefore the initial primary.
;
; Prepared here:
;   - SuperUser is logon-ready
;   - MIRRORDATA database exists, journalled, ready to be added to the mirror
;   - MIRRORNS namespace over it, so data can be written and later checked on the
;     other member
;
; Deliberately NOT prepared - this is the exercise (see ../EXERCISE.md):
;   - %Service_Mirror is left disabled. It is off by default, and enabling it is
;     the first step of setting up a mirror.
;   - no mirror set exists
;
; ISCAgent needs no preparation: iris-main starts it automatically (its --ISCAgent
; argument defaults to true) and it listens on 2188 in every container.

[Actions]
ModifyUser:Name=SuperUser,ChangePassword=0

CreateDatabase:Name=MIRRORDATA,Directory=/usr/irissys/mgr/mirrordata

CreateNamespace:Name=MIRRORNS,Globals=MIRRORDATA,Routines=MIRRORDATA
